proposed_statement_changes.proposed:
For the full-design-centered subclass \(\mathcal M_{N,T,\mathbf n}^{\dagger}(\lambda)\), there are constants \(0<c<C<\infty\), depending only on fixed class and procedural constants, such that along every array with \(N\wedge T\wedge\min_s n_s\to\infty\), uniformly for \(P\) in that subclass and for almost every admissible realized path \(z_0\in\mathcal Z_+\),
\[
cR_{\star,\beta}
\le\inf_{\widetilde\tau}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{N,T,\mathbf n}^{\dagger}(\lambda)}
\mathbb E_P[(\widetilde\tau-\tau_n(z_0))^2\mid E_0]
\le\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{N,T,\mathbf n}^{\dagger}(\lambda)}
\mathbb E_P[(\widehat\tau-\tau_n(z_0))^2\mid E_0]
\le CR_{\star,\beta}.
\]
The raw estimator in \texttt{def:feasible-estimator}, using all donors once, the normalized-shape selector, and the log-adjusted initial bandwidth, attains the upper bound with nonidentically distributed bounded event and historical unit responses and an unknown non-Gaussian donor law with unrestricted coordinate heteroskedasticity inside the covariance envelope.  The estimator does not use or estimate \(\Sigma\).  No sequential-overlap or other anti-clustering assumption is imposed.

